00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.890
And the numbers for GDP for the first quarter
getting worse from four point eight percent

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.220
down to five percent down.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.270
A sign of what is to come.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.600
Now, jobs numbers.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.750
Last week, another two point one million people
lost their jobs.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:36.390
New unemployment claims last week, two point
one million new unin point unemployment claims

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:44.330
now understand that before coronavirus, 700000
job losses in a week was the record.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.250
I believe it was sometimes sometime in the
80s.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.190
I don't remember if it was 82 or 88.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:53.690
I've mentioned it before, but losing 700000
jobs in a week was the record for the United

00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:54.690
States.

00:01:54.690 --> 00:02:01.960
We've now had about 10 consecutive weeks of
anywhere from three to 10 times those numbers,

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.160
10 consecutive weeks.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.220
So we now have a first couple of weeks.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.180
It was about six million jobs lost each week,
then five million.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.130
Then around four million jobs for a couple
of weeks.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.820
Then we lost three million jobs a week for
a couple of weeks.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.210
And in total.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:23.300
Forty one million new unemployment claims
have been made during the era of Corona virus

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.940
the last 10 weeks.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.890
Remember that before Corona virus, we estimated
the labor force was about one hundred and

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.700
fifty eight million people.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.470
So that means that 26 percent of the total
workforce

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:38.310
in 10 weeks lost their jobs.

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:41.680
Insane, unimaginable economic destruction.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.670
Now, a few things to bear in mind.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:48.450
This doesn't mean that now 41 million people
are still out of work.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:53.240
Some of the people who lost their jobs, you
know, nine weeks ago, 10 weeks ago, they've

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.560
gotten new jobs.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.760
And in fact, if you look at continued claims,
ongoing unemployment claims, it actually has

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:00.760
come down.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:05.580
So two weeks ago, we were at 25 million active,
unemployed people.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.200
That is now down to twenty one million.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:09.850
So that's something.

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:14.660
It means that in the last week, more people
got off of unemployment than the number that

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.000
got on.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.420
The most likely scenario based on these numbers
is that we are going to see very high unemployment

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:27.420
numbers for a very long time, even if every
state was able to reopen today to 75 percent,

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:34.060
you would still see very big numbers continuing
certainly into 2021.

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.280
And there are questions about could this be,
you know, a two year recovery?

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.770
Could this be a five year recovery?

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.200
We just don't know.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:46.140
But the point is, forget about this being
fixed to any significant degree before the

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.360
November election.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:52.670
And this is why yesterday's segment about
garbage math is so important, because there

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:58.690
is a good chance that after disastrous second
quarter numbers, we will start to see some

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.210
improvement from these.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.210
Absolutely.

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:05.460
You know, bottom, bottom, bottom lows in the
third quarter.

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:10.170
And as we start to see that recovery in the
third quarter, hopefully if we just continue

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:16.359
straight on wave one and wave to blend together
and things continued to worsen, this may not

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:17.359
